1
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:47,658
Come on. I don't have all day.

2
00:01:48,192 --> 00:01:50,528
What'll it be, Ryo-san? She's limited edition.

3
00:01:50,728 --> 00:01:53,164
If you let her slip, she's gone for good.

4
00:01:53,564 --> 00:01:54,632
I'll pay you back.

5
00:01:54,832 --> 00:01:56,200
Absolutely not.

6
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:59,069
You've been in credit since the year before last.

7
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:00,171
You pay in cash.

8
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:03,374
You can move on if you're not serious.

9
00:02:03,574 --> 00:02:06,177
I have plenty of other paying customers.

10
00:02:06,377 --> 00:02:07,378
Damn it.

11
00:02:07,578 --> 00:02:09,513
Kicking me when I'm down, huh?

12
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:11,282
Guess I have no choice...

13
00:02:13,217 --> 00:02:14,385
Take it, you thief!

14
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:16,187
Thanks, as always!

15
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,523
Haha! I did it! I did it!

16
00:02:25,362 --> 00:02:26,730
Hmm...

17
00:02:27,097 --> 00:02:30,234
Maybe I should have pushed for at least half credit.

18
00:02:30,434 --> 00:02:32,736
Now I've got no money left.

19
00:02:33,103 --> 00:02:35,906
How am I going to make it until payday?

20
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:39,210
Well, first I'll have to pass on that work trip...

21
00:02:39,410 --> 00:02:40,044
Hmm?

22
00:02:42,012 --> 00:02:43,047
The work trip, huh?

23
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:45,883
All right!

24
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,051
"LUXURY CRUISE TRIP"

25
00:02:47,484 --> 00:02:48,285
What?!

26
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:52,289
The Katsushika Police recreational trip?

27
00:02:52,957 --> 00:02:54,291
You're gonna organize it?

28
00:02:54,959 --> 00:02:57,061
Will you take it seriously, Ryo-chan?

29
00:02:57,695 --> 00:02:58,562
I will and I am.

30
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:00,764
I've decided to volunteer.

31
00:03:00,965 --> 00:03:04,401
I'm gonna do my part for all my colleagues.

32
00:03:04,802 --> 00:03:07,404
Good for you, Ryo-sama. You're so considerate.

33
00:03:07,738 --> 00:03:11,575
But you complain every year about how expensive it is.

34
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:12,409
Huh?

35
00:03:12,943 --> 00:03:17,147
And you're always saying organizers only get to drink half as much alcohol.

36
00:03:17,648 --> 00:03:21,485
You're up to something, aren't you, Ryotsu?

37
00:03:21,719 --> 00:03:22,419
Gulp...

38
00:03:23,187 --> 00:03:24,321
I am not!

39
00:03:24,522 --> 00:03:30,160
Remember last year's work trip? When the chief was the organizer?

40
00:03:31,262 --> 00:03:36,133
Why, on a Sunday, of all days, would he take us to an amusement park?

41
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:39,603
We were there half the day and only got to ride two rides.

42
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:41,338
And the food was terrible.

43
00:03:41,538 --> 00:03:44,508
Small portions, tasted bland, and there was no dessert.

44
00:03:44,942 --> 00:03:47,478
Then there was that karaoke contest at the end.

45
00:03:47,678 --> 00:03:51,348
They only had one song by my favorite artist, Hachigoro Kasuga.

46
00:03:51,549 --> 00:03:54,285
The microphone broke, and we all got kicked out.

47
00:03:54,652 --> 00:03:56,287
The day was a total failure.

48
00:03:56,487 --> 00:04:00,190
The microphone broke because you sang too loudly,

49
00:04:00,391 --> 00:04:03,527
and we got kicked out because you caused a scene.

50
00:04:03,761 --> 00:04:04,762
Rookie!

51
00:04:04,962 --> 00:04:09,033
A good event organizer should have known that I tend to sing loudly.

52
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,336
That's not something people generally know.

53
00:04:12,636 --> 00:04:14,104
You're a rookie too!

54
00:04:14,305 --> 00:04:15,673
Such an amateur, Nakagawa!

55
00:04:15,873 --> 00:04:20,344
A good event organizer anticipates every possible scenario.

56
00:04:20,778 --> 00:04:24,648
Having the chief organize the day was the root of all our problems.

57
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:26,984
An amusement park, dinner, and karaoke?

58
00:04:27,184 --> 00:04:28,886
What a stock-standard itinerary.

59
00:04:29,119 --> 00:04:30,988
Not a shred of taste.

60
00:04:31,188 --> 00:04:35,559
No unimaginative paint-by-numbers type could ever organize a good event—

61
00:04:36,327 --> 00:04:38,963
Uh, no, I mean...

62
00:04:41,265 --> 00:04:42,499
Chief!

63
00:04:43,067 --> 00:04:45,502
I hear you loud and clear.

64
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:49,740
You mean to say you're skipping out on our next work trip!

65
00:04:49,974 --> 00:04:53,510
No, I'm not skipping out. I'm going to organize it!

66
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,980
You? An organizer? Don't make me laugh!

67
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:56,981
I'm doing it!

68
00:04:57,181 --> 00:04:59,216
I'll do it for 5,000 yen per person,

69
00:04:59,416 --> 00:05:01,919
and it'll be so much better than any of yours!

70
00:05:02,286 --> 00:05:03,921
I don't believe you.

71
00:05:04,722 --> 00:05:05,456
I can do it!

72
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:07,024
No you can't!

73
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:08,258
Yes I can!

74
00:05:10,894 --> 00:05:12,630
I believe in you, Ryo-sama!

75
00:05:13,397 --> 00:05:16,166
Fine. You think you can do it? Go ahead!

76
00:05:16,367 --> 00:05:19,203
But if I'm bored even once on this trip,

77
00:05:19,403 --> 00:05:22,106
I'll dock the expenses out of your pay!

78
00:05:24,842 --> 00:05:25,843
Fine.

79
00:05:26,043 --> 00:05:28,479
But if it turns out to be a hoot,

80
00:05:28,712 --> 00:05:31,749
you'll cancel all those reports I'm supposed to write.

81
00:05:32,282 --> 00:05:36,286
Hmm, a fair deal. Here's the expenses and the participants.

82
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,322
He fell for it.

83
00:05:39,256 --> 00:05:40,190
"CUT-PRICE LUXURY CRUISE"

84
00:05:40,391 --> 00:05:41,291
What?!

85
00:05:43,594 --> 00:05:47,598
We're going on a cruise? With our budget?

86
00:05:47,798 --> 00:05:49,133
Leave it to me.

87
00:05:49,333 --> 00:05:51,635
I know people in all the right places.

88
00:05:51,869 --> 00:05:53,971
And that's just a little taste, okay?

89
00:05:54,471 --> 00:05:56,640
All right, off I go to organize!

90
00:05:57,641 --> 00:06:01,612
If it costs 1,000 yen per person, that's a 4,000 yen profit on each one.

91
00:06:01,812 --> 00:06:03,414
Ryo-chan, you're so smart!

92
00:06:11,488 --> 00:06:14,792
Dinner with a live band on a cruise ship.

93
00:06:14,992 --> 00:06:17,294
This year's trip is going to be so cool!

94
00:06:17,494 --> 00:06:18,429
Yeah!

95
00:06:18,629 --> 00:06:20,097
It's gonna be the bomb!

96
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:22,999
I've always wanted to go on a cruise.

97
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,369
I hope I don't get seasick.

98
00:06:25,602 --> 00:06:27,705
-You'll be fine. -Cruise ships don't rock.

99
00:06:27,938 --> 00:06:30,474
-Good morning! -Good morning, Superintendent.

100
00:06:30,674 --> 00:06:32,376
Oh, good morning, ladies.

101
00:06:32,609 --> 00:06:33,777
And hello, Ohara.

102
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:37,848
Yes, hello, sir. Thank you for joining us amid your busy schedule.

103
00:06:38,082 --> 00:06:39,683
Good morning!

104
00:06:39,917 --> 00:06:43,821
Well, how could I not? I heard this year's trip will be quite luxurious.

105
00:06:44,021 --> 00:06:47,024
Ryotsu may be a menace, but he organizes a good shindig.

106
00:06:47,257 --> 00:06:48,292
I suppose so.

107
00:06:48,492 --> 00:06:51,462
You think we'll be fine, Ohara?

108
00:06:51,662 --> 00:06:53,797
We'll be fine! Probably...

109
00:06:56,934 --> 00:07:01,038
But he is late. Even the superintendent, our guest of honor, is already here.

110
00:07:01,472 --> 00:07:04,475
-He said to meet at 10 a.m., right? -Yeah.

111
00:07:04,675 --> 00:07:07,745
But I don't see how we can afford a cruise with a live band

112
00:07:07,978 --> 00:07:10,280
on a budget of only 5,000 yen per person.

113
00:07:10,481 --> 00:07:11,181
Me neither.

114
00:07:11,381 --> 00:07:14,218
Hey, everyone! Sorry for the hold up!

115
00:07:14,551 --> 00:07:16,186
Oh, there he is.

116
00:07:16,587 --> 00:07:17,955
Look! Look at that boat!

117
00:07:26,497 --> 00:07:27,698
Wow, it's beautiful!

118
00:07:27,898 --> 00:07:29,133
Ryotsu did well!

119
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:31,001
What a gorgeous cruise ship.

120
00:07:31,201 --> 00:07:32,769
It's nicer than I thought!

121
00:07:33,003 --> 00:07:35,405
Hey! Over here!

122
00:07:42,012 --> 00:07:43,413
It went past us.

123
00:07:43,614 --> 00:07:45,916
Hey! Over here, over here!

124
00:07:46,416 --> 00:07:50,053
Chief! Guys! This is it!

125
00:07:52,689 --> 00:07:55,392
Eh?!

126
00:07:58,762 --> 00:08:00,864
Ryotsu! What is that?

127
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:04,334
Can't you tell? It's a houseboat.

128
00:08:04,535 --> 00:08:09,773
-I thought we were going on a cruise? -Yeah! This isn't what you promised!

129
00:08:10,007 --> 00:08:12,409
This is a bona fide Japanese cruise ship.

130
00:08:12,609 --> 00:08:14,778
Stop complaining and get on board!

131
00:08:17,481 --> 00:08:20,217
What do you think? Very Japanese, huh?

132
00:08:20,417 --> 00:08:21,919
The roof is full of holes.

133
00:08:22,119 --> 00:08:27,291
Right! So you don't have to go outside to sunbathe or get in touch with nature.

134
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:30,794
The tatami mats are worn out.

135
00:08:31,495 --> 00:08:32,362
Oh, Chief!

136
00:08:32,563 --> 00:08:34,898
Don't put too much weight there.

137
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:36,633
-It's rotten. -What?

138
00:08:37,034 --> 00:08:37,801
Huh?

139
00:08:38,035 --> 00:08:42,306
Come on, cheer up. Let's enjoy the trip.

140
00:08:42,506 --> 00:08:44,908
Ryotsu, this is not worth 5,000 yen.

141
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:46,577
But the food is worth it.

142
00:08:47,077 --> 00:08:51,848
He's right, Ohara. The boat may be old, but what really matters is the food.

143
00:08:52,082 --> 00:08:54,284
Fresh fish, am I right?

144
00:08:54,585 --> 00:08:55,853
That's right! Exactly!

145
00:08:56,086 --> 00:08:58,055
Fish is all about freshness!

146
00:08:58,255 --> 00:09:02,392
Now then. Everyone, let's get fishing.

147
00:09:02,593 --> 00:09:04,528
-What? -What's going on?

148
00:09:04,761 --> 00:09:05,796
What's this?

149
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:09,499
Did I forget to tell you? We're doing some luxury fishing.

150
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:11,168
Oh, right.

151
00:09:11,401 --> 00:09:14,805
Chief, Nakagawa, Honda, Reiko, and you traffic division girls,

152
00:09:15,005 --> 00:09:17,641
we're gonna cast our lines out to the open sea!

153
00:09:17,975 --> 00:09:20,844
No, Ryo-chan. We're not going fishing.

154
00:09:21,078 --> 00:09:21,845
No way!

155
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,348
Oh? That's too bad.

156
00:09:24,715 --> 00:09:25,549
What's too bad?

157
00:09:25,983 --> 00:09:29,786
Whatever we catch is going to be our dinner.

158
00:09:29,987 --> 00:09:31,321
Guess you don't want any.

159
00:09:31,788 --> 00:09:33,123
What?!

160
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:34,157
You can't!

161
00:09:34,558 --> 00:09:36,827
Everyone catches their own food.

162
00:09:37,027 --> 00:09:39,663
This is how we have fun on our work trip.

163
00:09:39,997 --> 00:09:43,100
If you don't, you'll just have to watch everyone else eat

164
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:45,168
while you twiddle your thumbs.

165
00:09:47,271 --> 00:09:50,107
Don't worry. We'll help you.

166
00:09:50,307 --> 00:09:51,041
Yeah.

167
00:09:51,875 --> 00:09:53,677
Thanks so much!

168
00:09:53,877 --> 00:09:55,512
You're so nice!

169
00:09:55,979 --> 00:09:57,147
Unlike you.

170
00:09:57,581 --> 00:09:59,149
Hmph. Did I hear something?

171
00:10:03,153 --> 00:10:07,224
Mmm... But just being out in the sea breeze feels lovely.

172
00:10:07,858 --> 00:10:09,860
This is actually pretty nice.

173
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:11,228
Oh! I got a bite!

174
00:10:12,229 --> 00:10:13,730
Hmm? It's a big one!

175
00:10:15,565 --> 00:10:16,767
Here it comes!

176
00:10:19,336 --> 00:10:20,370
Look! I caught one!

177
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:22,139
Well done! You're good!

178
00:10:22,339 --> 00:10:25,042
Ryo-sama, I've got a bite too!

179
00:10:25,242 --> 00:10:26,376
Oh! Me too!

180
00:10:28,412 --> 00:10:31,048
Oh, a black porgy! Nice work, Maria.

181
00:10:31,415 --> 00:10:33,383
Me too...! Here it comes!

182
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:35,152
Huh?

183
00:10:41,024 --> 00:10:42,359
All right, I caught one!

184
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:46,229
Hope you're all having fun.

185
00:10:46,630 --> 00:10:49,633
Oh, Honda. All you've caught are gobies.

186
00:10:50,167 --> 00:10:52,235
Yeah. Not sure why.

187
00:10:52,602 --> 00:10:55,739
Well, that's okay. Fried gobies are delicious.

188
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,107
Hmm?

189
00:10:57,808 --> 00:11:01,378
What's going on, Chief? You haven't caught anything yet.

190
00:11:01,979 --> 00:11:03,880
Shut up. It'll happen any moment.

191
00:11:04,448 --> 00:11:07,884
Even Terai and the traffic division girls have caught something.

192
00:11:08,285 --> 00:11:12,389
Shouldn't a man of your league be catching tuna or whale by now?

193
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:13,990
Oww!

194
00:11:14,891 --> 00:11:17,561
Hey, I'm not fish!

195
00:11:17,761 --> 00:11:20,063
Stop it with the tuna and the whales.

196
00:11:20,263 --> 00:11:23,900
Anyway, Ryotsu. Aren't you going to fish for your dinner?

197
00:11:24,101 --> 00:11:25,535
Nope. I'm the organizer.

198
00:11:26,303 --> 00:11:28,772
I'll take my share from everyone else.

199
00:11:28,972 --> 00:11:32,809
After all, being the organizer comes with its own lot of hardships.

200
00:11:33,009 --> 00:11:37,547
Ryo-sama! I'll catch some for you!

201
00:11:38,482 --> 00:11:42,319
But remember, there'll be no dinner for you if you don't catch anything.

202
00:11:42,853 --> 00:11:46,690
Hmph. I spent 5,000 yen just to have to catch my own fish to eat...

203
00:11:46,923 --> 00:11:48,258
Oh! Another one!

204
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:51,595
Haha, this is pretty fun. Wouldn't you say, Ohara?

205
00:11:51,795 --> 00:11:52,829
Y-Yes, sir....

206
00:11:55,132 --> 00:11:56,233
Oh! I got something!

207
00:11:57,401 --> 00:11:59,269
It's a big one!

208
00:11:59,469 --> 00:12:00,704
Hang in there, Ohara!

209
00:12:02,439 --> 00:12:03,940
You can do it, Chief!

210
00:12:05,142 --> 00:12:06,143
Keep going!

211
00:12:06,343 --> 00:12:09,946
Amazing! You might've caught enough for everyone, Chief.

212
00:12:10,147 --> 00:12:11,481
Stop talking and help!

213
00:12:11,681 --> 00:12:12,449
Oh, okay.

214
00:12:14,351 --> 00:12:16,253
This is incredible, Chief!

215
00:12:16,453 --> 00:12:18,989
-Ryotsu, I won't let it get away! -Okay!

216
00:12:26,062 --> 00:12:26,897
Chief!

217
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:28,465
I did it!

218
00:12:32,035 --> 00:12:33,370
A ship's rudder?

219
00:12:33,870 --> 00:12:35,539
What are you doing, Chief?

220
00:12:35,739 --> 00:12:38,875
Instead of a rudderfish, you fished out a rudder!

221
00:12:39,976 --> 00:12:43,880
But Ryotsu, isn't that rudder part of this boat...?

222
00:12:45,215 --> 00:12:47,884
Don't worry, you guys! Keep fishing!

223
00:12:50,854 --> 00:12:53,623
I can't believe he fished up the boat's rudder.

224
00:12:54,157 --> 00:12:55,759
I'd better hide it.

225
00:12:57,461 --> 00:12:58,829
Oh, damn it!

226
00:13:01,064 --> 00:13:02,466
This isn't funny at all.

227
00:13:02,666 --> 00:13:04,301
That was pretty fun, though.

228
00:13:04,501 --> 00:13:06,203
Fishing is easy!

229
00:13:06,670 --> 00:13:08,572
Well, great work, everyone.

230
00:13:08,772 --> 00:13:11,174
Come on in and sit down.

231
00:13:11,675 --> 00:13:13,210
Huh?

232
00:13:15,078 --> 00:13:17,481
Chief, here. This is the best seat.

233
00:13:17,681 --> 00:13:21,117
Hey, the superintendent should sit here.

234
00:13:21,651 --> 00:13:25,589
Don't be so formal. We're on a casual outing.

235
00:13:25,789 --> 00:13:30,060
And the superintendent is our guest. You're the main man on this trip.

236
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:31,127
But still...

237
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:34,664
He's right, Ohara. Don't be shy.

238
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:39,402
But something feels cold on my backside.

239
00:13:39,803 --> 00:13:41,571
Don't worry about that.

240
00:13:41,771 --> 00:13:44,941
Now, Chief. No matter what happens, stay put.

241
00:13:45,142 --> 00:13:47,911
Don't move from this seat.

242
00:13:48,612 --> 00:13:50,881
Let's give the Chief a round of applause!

243
00:14:04,394 --> 00:14:05,095
So good!

244
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,166
The fried goby is tasty too.

245
00:14:15,105 --> 00:14:17,307
-Chief, if you'd like, you can have— -No!

246
00:14:17,541 --> 00:14:19,309
Is everyone having fun?

247
00:14:19,709 --> 00:14:21,845
Yeah!

248
00:14:23,079 --> 00:14:25,015
Let's get this party started!

249
00:14:25,248 --> 00:14:27,117
Bottoms up. There's plenty of sake.

250
00:14:27,918 --> 00:14:33,623
Now, for the big moment... A karaoke contest accompanied by a live band!

251
00:14:42,732 --> 00:14:44,634
Wait, isn't that the skipper?

252
00:14:45,101 --> 00:14:49,339
Yeah. He used to do musical comedy at Asakusa Rock back in the day.

253
00:14:49,573 --> 00:14:52,642
That's all well and good, but who's steering the boat?

254
00:14:52,842 --> 00:14:56,346
Huh? Oh, don't worry. It's on autopilot.

255
00:14:56,846 --> 00:14:58,148
Autopilot?

256
00:14:58,348 --> 00:15:00,850
This old boat has that sort of thing?

257
00:15:01,218 --> 00:15:03,853
I'm starting to worry. I'll go check.

258
00:15:04,054 --> 00:15:06,990
No, Chief! Don't move! You mustn't move.

259
00:15:07,190 --> 00:15:08,625
Get off me!

260
00:15:09,759 --> 00:15:11,161
You! What did you do?

261
00:15:11,528 --> 00:15:15,065
Chief, it's your fault. I told you not to move from there.

262
00:15:15,298 --> 00:15:16,166
Damn it, Ryotsu!

263
00:15:18,902 --> 00:15:20,604
-Ryotsu! -Get back here, Ryotsu!

264
00:15:23,373 --> 00:15:26,042
Ryotsu, we're going to sink!

265
00:15:26,443 --> 00:15:27,143
What?

266
00:15:27,344 --> 00:15:28,178
Ryotsu!

267
00:15:28,378 --> 00:15:29,546
Bail out the water!

268
00:15:40,457 --> 00:15:41,224
Oh, man.

269
00:15:41,458 --> 00:15:43,026
Don't give me "Oh, man"!

270
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:45,161
Ryotsu!

271
00:15:51,167 --> 00:15:54,504
Do something, Ryotsu!

272
00:16:15,925 --> 00:16:17,927
This side is fixed.

273
00:16:18,862 --> 00:16:22,599
Jeez, Chief. You've ruined our pleasant cruise.

274
00:16:22,832 --> 00:16:26,102
It's all your fault for booking such a rickety boat.

275
00:16:26,603 --> 00:16:28,605
It's rocking pretty violently.

276
00:16:29,305 --> 00:16:31,408
Oh, the rain's started to leak in.

277
00:16:40,383 --> 00:16:42,886
We may as well be outside.

278
00:16:44,421 --> 00:16:46,156
What's going on, Ryotsu?

279
00:16:46,389 --> 00:16:49,993
Don't worry. I brought umbrellas for just this kind of situation.

280
00:16:50,226 --> 00:16:51,394
Oh, that's thoughtful.

281
00:16:51,594 --> 00:16:54,898
However, they're rentals. So it's 200 yen each.

282
00:16:55,265 --> 00:16:56,299
What?

283
00:16:56,533 --> 00:16:58,134
I don't need one then!

284
00:17:04,641 --> 00:17:06,076
It's turned into a storm.

285
00:17:06,276 --> 00:17:07,410
No way, really?

286
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,411
Oh no!

287
00:17:08,978 --> 00:17:10,914
Ryotsu, we should go back to shore.

288
00:17:11,247 --> 00:17:12,782
Don't say that!

289
00:17:12,982 --> 00:17:15,151
Boats are supposed to rock.

290
00:17:15,352 --> 00:17:16,319
Hey, what's wrong?

291
00:17:16,553 --> 00:17:19,422
I think I'm getting seasick. I feel nauseous...

292
00:17:19,923 --> 00:17:21,458
You just need more alcohol!

293
00:17:21,991 --> 00:17:25,462
No time for feeling seasick when you're drunk.

294
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:27,997
This is a mess.

295
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:29,966
I know! Karaoke!

296
00:17:30,333 --> 00:17:32,268
A karaoke party to forget the storm!

297
00:17:32,469 --> 00:17:34,671
First, if I may, I'll sing a song.

298
00:17:35,004 --> 00:17:38,441
Gyujiro Ishihara's "The Gourmet Who Calls Forth a Storm."

299
00:17:39,509 --> 00:17:40,677
Man, it's rough.

300
00:17:41,578 --> 00:17:44,013
-We're in trouble, Ryo-san. -Yeah.

301
00:17:44,214 --> 00:17:44,948
I'll go too.

302
00:17:45,348 --> 00:17:48,918
A large low-pressure system is approaching the Kanto region.

303
00:17:49,285 --> 00:17:51,788
Vessels at sea should exercise caution.

304
00:17:51,988 --> 00:17:54,958
Heavy rain, flooding, and strong winds are expected.

305
00:17:55,158 --> 00:17:56,126
This is bad.

306
00:17:56,326 --> 00:17:57,927
What the heck's going on?

307
00:17:58,128 --> 00:18:00,997
For 5,000 yen per person, the service is terrible!

308
00:18:01,197 --> 00:18:02,932
What? 5,000? But I only got—

309
00:18:05,401 --> 00:18:08,171
Just have a drink. No holds barred!

310
00:18:08,371 --> 00:18:12,675
Screw it! Let the damn rain come!

311
00:18:13,042 --> 00:18:14,077
You moron.

312
00:18:14,310 --> 00:18:16,946
If the skipper gets drunk, who's going to steer?

313
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:20,083
It's fine. I can do it.

314
00:18:20,316 --> 00:18:24,420
This is where my hobbies come in handy. Watch.

315
00:18:25,622 --> 00:18:27,190
You moron!

316
00:18:27,390 --> 00:18:29,392
Ryo-chan's done something again.

317
00:18:29,626 --> 00:18:31,227
Don't make me think about it!

318
00:18:31,861 --> 00:18:34,230
The boat's moving further upstream.

319
00:18:46,009 --> 00:18:47,544
The river's getting narrower.

320
00:18:48,378 --> 00:18:51,414
We've left the Sumida River and entered the Kanda River!

321
00:18:51,648 --> 00:18:52,348
What?

322
00:18:59,689 --> 00:19:01,658
We're being swept away.

323
00:19:01,858 --> 00:19:06,229
Compared to a regular boat, this one's like a little bamboo raft.

324
00:19:06,429 --> 00:19:07,464
Oh no!

325
00:19:18,708 --> 00:19:20,710
There goes the roof.

326
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:23,379
Sorry, Ryotsu, but this is too dangerous.

327
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,882
I'm calling on the Nakagawa Corporation.

328
00:19:26,115 --> 00:19:27,550
Hello? It's me!

329
00:19:29,786 --> 00:19:30,920
Oh no!

330
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,155
We're done for.

331
00:19:38,862 --> 00:19:43,066
What's going to happen to us? What fate lies in store?

332
00:19:43,266 --> 00:19:44,567
I hate this!

333
00:19:44,934 --> 00:19:48,805
Turn those frowns upside down! Surprises are what make it fun!

334
00:19:49,038 --> 00:19:53,476
That's the best thing about travel. This is how we have fun on our work trip.

335
00:19:56,145 --> 00:20:00,250
We're gonna capsize! Bail out the water. We need to balance the boat!

336
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:03,453
Reiko, move to the center. Nakagawa, Chief, to the left.

337
00:20:03,653 --> 00:20:06,489
Everyone else, split into two and bail, bail, bail!

338
00:20:06,890 --> 00:20:07,924
Hurry, hurry!

339
00:20:08,424 --> 00:20:09,993
How have we not sunk yet?

340
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:13,630
If we survive, you'll regret ever being born, Ryotsu.

341
00:20:17,634 --> 00:20:19,802
Whoa! What a thrill!

342
00:20:26,910 --> 00:20:27,677
Look out!

343
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,648
Oh my gosh!

344
00:20:46,829 --> 00:20:50,199
-Ryotsu! A red light! -Do something, Ryotsu.

345
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,401
I'm on it!

346
00:20:57,540 --> 00:20:59,208
Whew, that was close.

347
00:20:59,409 --> 00:21:00,944
Why didn't you stop?

348
00:21:01,144 --> 00:21:02,545
We can't stop!

349
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:07,383
Look. The propeller shaft is broken.

350
00:21:07,584 --> 00:21:10,153
Ryotsu, the current is getting stronger.

351
00:21:10,353 --> 00:21:12,388
We're being sucked in by something!

352
00:21:12,589 --> 00:21:14,057
What? Oh!

353
00:21:14,424 --> 00:21:16,059
It's the subway entrance!

354
00:21:27,804 --> 00:21:29,372
We've gone onto the tracks!

355
00:21:30,573 --> 00:21:31,841
Look! Ryo-chan!

356
00:21:34,611 --> 00:21:37,614
Oh no! A train's coming!

357
00:21:41,718 --> 00:21:43,586
-Stop! -Stay back!

358
00:21:53,029 --> 00:21:54,364
We're safe...

359
00:21:54,831 --> 00:21:56,265
Not yet we aren't!

360
00:22:04,707 --> 00:22:06,776
Damn you, Ryotsu!

361
00:22:07,410 --> 00:22:11,014
Chief, what are you doing? This is no time for pulling faces.

362
00:22:11,214 --> 00:22:12,715
Just enjoy the ride!

363
00:22:13,182 --> 00:22:14,784
How can you enjoy this?

364
00:22:15,651 --> 00:22:17,420
Ugh, you're so mean!

365
00:22:18,021 --> 00:22:19,656
-You're mean! -Ouch, ouch, ouch!

366
00:22:20,790 --> 00:22:22,725
That's it, now you've done it.

367
00:22:22,925 --> 00:22:24,761
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

368
00:22:24,961 --> 00:22:26,496
How dare you!

369
00:22:27,463 --> 00:22:28,931
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

370
00:22:31,934 --> 00:22:34,670
As if they're really fighting at a time like this.

371
00:22:34,937 --> 00:22:35,938
I know.

372
00:22:38,941 --> 00:22:40,109
Oh! The outside!

373
00:22:40,309 --> 00:22:41,978
We've reached Ochanomizu!

374
00:23:07,236 --> 00:23:09,105
Well, Chief?

375
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:11,908
Were you bored even once on this trip?

376
00:23:12,275 --> 00:23:14,377
You... You moron...

377
00:23:15,478 --> 00:23:17,647
Hey, my boat may be old and shabby,

378
00:23:18,247 --> 00:23:21,651
but she's worth more than 1,000 yen per person.

379
00:23:21,984 --> 00:23:23,319
Ryotsu!

380
00:23:23,519 --> 00:23:24,353
Ryotsu.

381
00:23:24,554 --> 00:23:25,354
Ryo-chan!

382
00:23:25,655 --> 00:23:27,023
Ah, um...

383
00:23:27,256 --> 00:23:28,524
Explain yourself!

384
00:23:28,724 --> 00:23:31,527
Well, um, the thing is...

385
00:23:32,128 --> 00:23:34,397
Ryotsu! I knew something wasn't right.

386
00:23:34,630 --> 00:23:37,500
You pocketed the travel expenses, didn't you?

387
00:23:38,034 --> 00:23:39,135
Wait, wait!

388
00:23:41,471 --> 00:23:42,939
My money!

389
00:23:43,139 --> 00:23:43,840
Hey, Ryotsu!

390
00:23:45,208 --> 00:23:46,342
Ryotsu!

391
00:23:47,143 --> 00:23:48,945
My money... My money...

392
00:23:49,145 --> 00:23:50,346
You big moron!

393
00:23:50,546 --> 00:23:53,216
Let's cool that head of yours with a little dunk!

394
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:55,651
Stop it, Chief!

395
00:23:55,852 --> 00:23:57,520
My money!

396
00:24:02,959 --> 00:24:08,765
RYO-SAN THE MATCH-BREAKER
